# spectral-norm over typed arrays: each product with A is one vector
# tabulated over its rows, each row the sum of its products with the
# vector, whose bodies only compute, so they are structured; after the
# vectorization the rows compute on the target's lanes, each lane summing
# its row in index order, and after idr-narrow-lanes every loop computing
# 64-bit integer lanes is the 64-bit version beside one computing its
# index arithmetic in 32 bits. The structuring and the vectorization group
# each run over the functions in a group, which dumps no module: each
# property is read at the first step after its group.
eliminate-empty-tensors: structured-loops
idr-returned-arguments: vectorized narrowed-lanes
